    "warnings": [
      "Both theorems admit an empty vertex type with any d > 0: regularity is then vacuous, both threshold conditions hold, and the empty line graph is d-colourable, but its chromatic index is 0 rather than d. The stated d-edge-colourability agrees with Lean; the unqualified identification with χ′(G) = d does not. Qualify that equality as applying to nonempty graphs in the prose, or restrict the Lean statements if the equality is intended for every admitted case."
    ]
